# Who has to look before it merges (docs/decisions/review-gate.md, #108).
#
# Two directories hold the code that moves money or gates it: the escrow
# contracts and the compliance circuit. A pull request that touches either
# needs an approving review from one of the owners below who did not author
# it; everything else merges on green checks alone, as before. Branch
# protection enforces this through "require review from code owners"
# (docs/ci/branch-protection.json); this file only says who the owners are.
#
# The second owner on each line is the reviewer of the first: the person who
# writes most of a directory cannot approve their own pull request, and a
# rule with one owner would make every one of their changes wait on nobody.
# Owners must have write access; all three do.

